      "content": "This is a legitimate dilemma in urban design, but it is not an inevitable outcome; experts argue that the technology itself can be neutral and depends entirely on governance and privacy laws. Solutions exist, such as strictly limiting data aggregation, prioritizing on-road transportation sensors over granular pedestrian tracking, and mandating \"data by design\" protocols that prevent cross-referencing personal identities. By keeping infrastructure public, open, and focused on ecological health rather than monitoring, proponents believe the focus can remain on community well-being without creating a tool for state control.",
